[{:db/id "q-36559/selection/0e000855eb2a4331aa11e189e87d239c6a982a95767bf6ceea78fb40f972d372" :answer/id #uuid "a2331820-11ea-55ae-88cb-bd07dfd447cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12\\pi +6{\\pi }^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36559/selection/f1b5cb3d8bc923fc6ccfcab303169dfdca04af673b5f2d6422beb1c74f92922c" :answer/id #uuid "2505a76c-9b64-53f9-93a4-bb4a2f92a451" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\pi -6{\\pi }^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36559/selection/f53c30c025789a772c6d73061c15d481dbf3ce1d17202bb90459013da9f6616b" :answer/id #uuid "88dad69f-75f8-564b-9a7c-095bb57ae1ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6{\\pi }^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36559/selection/4640d9894fc183d803e4d1ca591f81c38201f2ce4a550e6f2de94fccffe28f6d" :answer/id #uuid "daaa23d7-6a82-5836-9e81-4c88515da490" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3{\\pi }^{3}-6{\\pi }^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36559/selection/3d822eee11b44fb963c12c1a743aa0d9e78eb0c887500bb593bbddd7ca3c8b23" :answer/id #uuid "516cf784-06ce-5301-a1ea-3a49c22759f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{\\pi }^{3}-6{\\pi }^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36559/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7223cee-7059-5272-8855-3a5d62726deb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-36559/selection/f53c30c025789a772c6d73061c15d481dbf3ce1d17202bb90459013da9f6616b" :answer-field/choices ["q-36559/selection/0e000855eb2a4331aa11e189e87d239c6a982a95767bf6ceea78fb40f972d372" "q-36559/selection/f1b5cb3d8bc923fc6ccfcab303169dfdca04af673b5f2d6422beb1c74f92922c" "q-36559/selection/f53c30c025789a772c6d73061c15d481dbf3ce1d17202bb90459013da9f6616b" "q-36559/selection/4640d9894fc183d803e4d1ca591f81c38201f2ce4a550e6f2de94fccffe28f6d" "q-36559/selection/3d822eee11b44fb963c12c1a743aa0d9e78eb0c887500bb593bbddd7ca3c8b23"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-36559" :question/id #uuid "8f246fa5-d146-527a-80ba-21dffbe00cb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-36559" :question/problem "Suppose that a function $f(x,y,z)$ and all of its higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ and that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂z}=3{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)+3x{y}^{2}z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz)+3{x}^{2}{z}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\n$$\n\nEvaluate the following expression at the point $(\\pi ,-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂z∂y∂y}+\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂y∂z∂z}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "As the higher order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂z∂y∂y} & =\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂y∂y∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)+3x{y}^{2}z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz)+3{x}^{2}{z}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =6y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)+6xyz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz)-3{x}^{3}{z}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn addition, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂y∂z∂z} & =\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂z∂y∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)+3x{y}^{2}z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz)+3{x}^{2}{z}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =3x{y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz)+3x{y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz)-3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)+6{x}^{2}z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate both partial derivatives at the point $(\\pi ,-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂z∂y∂y}{|}_{(\\pi ,-1,1)} & =6(-1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+6(\\pi )(-1)(1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-3(\\pi )^{3}(1)^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )=6\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂y∂z∂z}{|}_{(\\pi ,-1,1)} & =3(\\pi )(-1)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+3(\\pi )(-1)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-3(\\pi )^{2}(-1)^{2}(1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+6(\\pi )^{2}(1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )=-6\\pi -6{\\pi }^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂z∂y∂y}{|}_{(\\pi ,-1,1)}+\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂y∂z∂z}{|}_{(\\pi ,-1,1)} & =6\\pi +(-6\\pi -6{\\pi }^{2})=-6{\\pi }^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-36559/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7619454-7a2b-5c0b-927c-24dca2e564c3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36559"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80652/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "97f935ac-dc65-581a-8690-483db1565e10" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80652/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "cf78341f-bfae-5945-bdc7-43b516000b99" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80652/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "bcbdae4c-ce01-5d34-aae9-6e924fc99290" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80652/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "a0a7b7d5-564f-5ed1-abd4-652d463d486d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80652/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "fdd65fbd-e573-541c-83cb-336af378b312" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80652/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ff9459e8-8590-5381-b76e-8e4952daa8ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80652/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-80652/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-80652/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-80652/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-80652/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-80652/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80652" :question/id #uuid "24df999b-6ea6-5095-ada6-d510b0d36076" :question/math-academy-id "q-80652" :question/problem "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)=4x+{y}^{2}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=4xy-y$\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)=2x+y$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=x+\\sqrt{y}$\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)=2xy+{y}^{2}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)={x}^{2}y+2x$" :question/worked-solution "Since the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal, that is, ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y).$ Let's check if this condition is true for each of our pairs of first-order partial derivatives.\n\n- For the first pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4x+{y}^{2})=2y \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4xy-y)=4y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)\\ne {f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the first pair cannot represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the second pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x+y)=1 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+\\sqrt{y})=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the second pair could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the third pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy+{y}^{2})=2x+2y \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y+2x)=2xy+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)\\ne {f}_{yx}(x,y)$,  the third pair cannot represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'II only'." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80652/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b15f59e-ef74-5fa2-9af9-448fdcbbbd3d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80652"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80759/selection/b1a9f2bb9f9bd59b66c906c9ab98446a26ec623744a7f92356bb121785f6cea5" :answer/id #uuid "ddefbf88-4721-55c3-adae-d4153e8655f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80759/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "2274cd41-3523-5a35-9d10-a95f1b5d68b9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80759/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "dc93e348-c255-5eb5-84cc-29131719c035" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80759/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "24f7aa4e-f60b-5b4c-a54a-ae8a9f37919b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80759/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "922488ec-8953-5175-a96b-127f4cee91db" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80759/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a500767d-0118-5c50-971c-18ecc5932da8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80759/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-80759/selection/b1a9f2bb9f9bd59b66c906c9ab98446a26ec623744a7f92356bb121785f6cea5" "q-80759/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-80759/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-80759/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-80759/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80759" :question/id #uuid "57d651ac-3b25-5475-a085-e67636d23e90" :question/math-academy-id "q-80759" :question/problem "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)={e}^{-2x}-y$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)={e}^{-y}-2x$\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=5$\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)=2{y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡xy+{y}^{2}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡xy+2xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡xy+2xy$" :question/worked-solution "Since the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal, that is, ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y).$ Let's check if this condition is true for each of our pairs of first-order partial derivatives.\n\n- For the first pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{-2x}-y)=-1 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{-y}-2x)=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)\\ne {f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the first pair cannot represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the second pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=0 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(5)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the second pair could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the third pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡xy+{y}^{2})=4y\\operatorname{cos}⁡xy-2x{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡xy+2y \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡xy+2xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡xy+2xy) \\\\  & =2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡xy+2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡xy-2x{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡xy+2y \\\\  & =4y\\operatorname{cos}⁡xy-2x{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡xy+2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y)$,  the third pair could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'II and III only'." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-80759/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b15f59e-ef74-5fa2-9af9-448fdcbbbd3d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80759"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80762/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "95d3589a-79c5-52dc-8e5f-a2638bf4ea3d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80762/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "9847fbb0-5a77-53aa-af44-10d88774bed9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80762/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "13de481a-4365-5dce-b38e-460b9ed27555" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80762/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "7aee5159-636e-5fe7-8337-ab6921672655" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80762/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "84a726a4-30dd-5575-acf0-50d0b20dde51" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80762/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "95d3d35c-615b-5331-841e-ed31636d7701" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80762/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-80762/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-80762/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-80762/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-80762/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-80762/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80762" :question/id #uuid "813fc330-f1d0-5e6c-9e4f-df4f6cf7d2b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-80762" :question/problem "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)=2x-2{y}^{2}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=2y-2xy$\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{x})$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)={e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)=3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=2{x}^{3}y-\\sqrt{y}$" :question/worked-solution "Since the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal, that is, ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y).$ Let's check if this condition is true for each of our pairs of first-order partial derivatives.\n\n- For the first pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x-2{y}^{2})=-4y \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y-2xy)=-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)\\ne {f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the first pair cannot represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the second pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{x}))=0 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the second pair could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the third pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}{y}^{2})=6{x}^{2}y \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{3}y-\\sqrt{y})=6{x}^{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y)$,  the third pair could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'II and III only'." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80762/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b15f59e-ef74-5fa2-9af9-448fdcbbbd3d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80762"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-133373/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "04f5b191-6c29-5678-99dc-f9e7a2671d35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-133373/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "69b606c9-0e08-5d03-979e-ed29c0f0169b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-133373/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" :answer/id #uuid "53bf4a48-ada8-5510-971e-c00135eeef3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-133373/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "e48ae0d7-e2a3-54ef-8912-2be0952dc224" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-133373/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "e0277310-9c11-570c-a604-eeded6955db4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-133373/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4e20f6bb-bccd-5986-afdc-f8f5c8c5c714" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-133373/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-133373/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-133373/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-133373/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" "q-133373/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-133373/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-133373" :question/id #uuid "37ec63d6-7b9e-5cc5-b3cc-774fccb68297" :question/math-academy-id "q-133373" :question/problem "Given that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ evaluate ${f}_{yxy}(6,\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ if ${f}_{xy}(x,y)=7+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$" :question/worked-solution "As the higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yxy}(x,y) & ={f}_{xyy}(x,y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{xy}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(7+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(6,\\frac{\\pi }{3}):$\n\n$$\n{f}_{yxy}(6,\\frac{\\pi }{3})=6\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=3\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-133373/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7619454-7a2b-5c0b-927c-24dca2e564c3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-133373"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
